cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "what-for-and-how: two-engine intent excavation with terminus-based stopping and pluggable culture-packs"
abstract: "An agent skill with a universal engine and pluggable culture-packs that runs two phases before any plan, recommendation, or causal read lands. Phase 1 drills What for layer by layer until it reaches a terminus defined by the property of the last link, not a fixed count, using two distinct engines: a private-longing engine for a person's inner motive (guarded by zero hallucination) and a structural-logic engine for an observed system (guarded by split node and link evidence). Phase 2 bridges from the terminus back to the surface question, executing step 1 for personal cases and offering a strategic read for observed systems. Includes a tier-0 router, an input parser for sarcasm, masked subjects, language-relative subjecthood, and pre-attribution, a clinical-handoff brake, a relational and role-bound terminus, and proposals spoken aloud as debts. The culture-bound terminus map, speech-act repertoire, and parser signals load from a culture-pack; Vietnamese is the first reference pack. Hardened by a model comparison, a 1000-case simulated stress audit, a multi-council linguistic and cultural critique, and a dogfood."
type: software
